Attack 2 — sentinel collisions.
  (a) User-named phase literally "-": cosmetically indistinguishable from
      "no phase" either way (pre- and post-Z5); not a Z5-introduced defect,
      not pursued further.
  (b) Enabled-but-unnamed phase (Phases[i].Name == "" with Enabled: true):
      GetSpendingPhaseNameAt returns "" for this case too (whatif.go:471-483
      only special-cases nil/disabled/empty-slice, not an empty Name string
      on a real phase). Reproduced empirically
      (TestZ5CheckerProbe_EnabledButUnnamedPhaseCollidesWithSentinel,
      discarded): engine records "-" for this config, where pre-Z5 it
      recorded "" (silently absent, no dash). Checked reachability: grepped
      handlers_rates.go's phase-save handler (line 142) — `if name :=
      r.FormValue(nameKey); name != "" { phase.Name = name }` — a blank
      posted name field falls through to the PRE-EXISTING base phase name
      (never blank, sourced from DefaultSpendingPhases() or the current
      config), so the UI structurally cannot produce this state; no JSON
      settings-import handler was found either. Not reachable via any
      consumer this task or its siblings touch. FINDING for the backlog,
      not a FAIL basis (unreachable, and the display difference is
      cosmetic — blank cell vs. a dash — even if reached).

Attack 3 — split-classification: two independent `"-"` literals exist,
  engine/stepper.go's `noPhaseSentinel` and handler
  spending_trajectory.go's `trajectoryPhaseName`'s `return "-"`. Currently
  they agree by construction and are exactly what lead ruling D-Z-f
  specified verbatim ("the engine records the literal no-phase token `-`
  ... handler preference logic unchanged"), so this is the approved design,
  not a worker deviation. FINDING for the backlog (a shared exported
  constant would remove future-drift risk) — not a FAIL basis: no observable
  divergence today, and the acceptance criteria did not ask for a shared
  constant.

Attack 4 — other consumers of PhaseName: grepped every phase_name/PhaseName
  site repo-wide. web/templates/components/kpis.html and
  portfolio-settings.html read a DIFFERENT PhaseName (budget_fit.go /
  living_expenses_phase_note.go, calling GetSpendingPhaseNameAt directly,
  untouched by Z5) — no sentinel leaks there. mcpsvc/plan/view.go's
  YearView does not carry PhaseName at all — no MCP leak. Confirmed only
  one true ProjectionYearSummary constructor site touches the stepper's
  CurrentPhaseName (month.go's runMonthlyLoop); explainability.go's
  fallback-rebuild path builds a separate LOCAL summaries slice (never
  assigned back to proj.YearlySummaries) so it cannot leak "" into
  buildSpendingTrajectoryRows. Both RunFast and RunFull
  (orchestrator.go) call the same eng.Run(in) -> runMonthlyLoop, so the
  production spending-trajectory handler (analysisFastOrCached ->
  RunFast) always gets a stepper-populated projection, not Monte Carlo.

